  "caveats": [
    "2026-10-20確認時の履歴: Maintainer fields and prose identify 2026.10.18 as the fix, while Reviewed structured fixed is 2026.10.19. Reviewed prose itself says .18 removed all emSign roots and .19 restored only unaffected roots. Both PyPI releases exist; checksum-verified wheel bundles confirm .18 has no emSign root labels and .19 has G1/C1/C3 but not the implicated ECC G3. Use .18 as the issue-specific first fix boundary, preserve Reviewed .19 raw, and do not mistake .19 restoration for reintroduction of the implicated root.",
    "The Reviewed narrative recommends 2026.10.19 or later. An issue-specific first fix boundary is not a claim that .18 is the preferred current upgrade target. Root-label checks are corroboration, not an independent cryptographic audit of the CA incident.",
    "The source says emSign roots were removed because intermediate keys were compromised; do not infer a specific company incident or observed MITM from that library advisory alone.",
    "Fixed database source and developer advisory were individually compared. Database and maintainer dates remain separately attributed.",
    "Exploitation and CISA KEV are unverified; unknown is not evidence of absence.",
    "2026-10-27 JST確認ではReviewedのfixedも2026.10.18へ訂正され、開発元の境界と一致した。以前に確認した.18と.19の証明書構成差・.19推奨の背景は履歴として保持する。",
    "固定Reviewedと開発元資料を個別照合。DBと開発元の公開・更新日時は出典別に保持する。",
    "実悪用とCISA KEVは未確認。未確認は悪用なし・未掲載を意味しない。"
  ],
